  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Samoa National Tripartite Forum (SNTF) was strengthened since the ratification of C144 in 2018. The SNTF met in 2019-2021 to discuss the ratification of ILO Conventions, including C81, C160, C187 and C190.   The SNTF supported the ratification of C190, C187 and C81 as a priority for Samoa.  Ratifications are planned by the end of 2021. C190 legal review was also presented and discussed by the SNTF in 2020. The SNTF regularly meets to discuss other agenda items. The ILO organised a number of capacity building sessions for the members of the SNTF in 2019-2021, including on the International Labour Standards and reporting.  It also gave a presentation and held discussions on the recommendations of the C190 review report in December 2020.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.3.2 Number of member States with tripartite mechanisms enabling constituents to effectively engage in the implementation of international labour standards at the national level, including reporting to the supervisory bodies</narrative>
